{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003166-non-kindred-vampires","id":1003166,"title":"Non-Kindred Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T17:50:04-08:00","id":1003166,"title":"Non-Kindred Vampires","content":"Let's say if this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire\">scenario</a> was true then I wonder if there's any vampire-like &quot;species&quot; or any alternatives to Kindred that exist in the Chronicles of Darkness? Especially a Undead corpse that is actually inhabited by the soul of the dead person instead of the beast parasite of the Kindred? Which means this particular vampire has no beast which means they can't frenzy nor do they have any humanity system at all, all they have to do is sustain themselves with blood or life sources to maintain their undead bodies. Especially these types of vampires don't embrace but instead they raise out of their graves or any place their corpse maybe laying at or maybe it's a result of a alchemical immortality ritual to become &quot;<a href=\"http://www.all-dao.com/immortality-achievements.html\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Immortals</a>&quot; hence they're self made into 'vampires'?<br /> <br /> Description below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. <b>Phantom-immortal or ghost-immortal - Gui Xian </b>( \u9b3c\u4ed9 )<br /> Gui Xian. Literally - the immortal among devils or the immortal devil. It was believed that this achievement is a characteristic of shamanic practices, the late Chan Buddhism, the pseudo-Taoism, different meditations. Withdrawal of Yin spirit in a state of no breath and palpitation. The practitioner remains mortal, despite the practice of spirit withdrawal and possible capabilities. Moreover, he may not be reborn after his death and stay a ghost forever. This was not practiced in Taoism, it was forbidden (meaning the serious study, not just jingzuo). </div> </div> </div>By the point is, if the scenario I've linked to is true, then I guess Requiem Kindred should not be playable at all and should be NPC only because it breaks the &quot;once human&quot; element of the game hence why I'm creating a new vampire race so that it would be actually <i>you</i> not something pretending to be you.<br /> <br /> Basically let's say I want to be a Vampire in a Chronicles of Darkness game but don't want to be Kindred due to these reasons so what other alternatives are available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-14-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T19:32:04-08:00","id":1003207,"title":"","content":"I always thought that Kindred <i>were </i>themselves, represented by the Humanity trait, and the Beast was their Id and base urges ramped up to supernatural potency by the shock of death and corrupted by the Curse. Draugr, Kindred whose Humanity eroded to nothingness, would be those &quot;corpses ridden around by a psychic parasite&quot; that you seem to view the entirety of the Kindred as.<br /> <br /> That said, how about Kudlak and Kresnik? Forgot which part of the globe they were from, but basically the former are evil witches whose astrally project their spirits each night that take on a animal form always black in color to cause misfortunes and drink human blood. The latter are good heroes who do the same astral projection, but in a white animal form, and combat Kudlak in the night.<br /> <br /> And how curious, the article you've linked to is quite different from what I knew about the Xian. But then again, I'm Korean and our Taoist myths probably don't match up with that in China. Nor do we have a orthodox 'canon' in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and the Kudlak and Kresnik are born in that state, often signified by a caul, so no worries about being Not Actually Human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T19:45:41-08:00","id":1003209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003166-non-kindred-vampires?p=1003207#post1003207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that Kindred <i>were </i>themselves, represented by the Humanity trait, and the Beast was their Id and base urges ramped up to supernatural potency by the shock of death and corrupted by the Curse. Draugr, Kindred whose Humanity eroded to nothingness, would be those &quot;corpses ridden around by a psychic parasite&quot; that you seem to view the entirety of the Kindred as.<br /> <br /> That said, how about Kudlak and Kresnik? Forgot which part of the globe they were from, but basically the former are evil witches whose astrally project their spirits each night that take on a animal form always black in color to cause misfortunes and drink human blood. The latter are good heroes who do the same astral projection, but in a white animal form, and combat Kudlak in the night.<br /> <br /> And how curious, the article you've linked to is quite different from what I knew about the Xian. But then again, I'm Korean and our Taoist myths probably don't match up with that in China. Nor do we have a orthodox 'canon' in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and the Kudlak and Kresnik are born in that state, often signified by a caul, so no worries about being Not Actually Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then again, I kinda prefer the Kindred being themselves but that thread though I've linked to just made me a little depressed as one of the reasons why I've created this thread though.<br /> <br /> Also how is the Xian different in Korea than the Chinese one I've linked to?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T22:30:56-08:00","id":1003255,"title":"","content":"So we're clear, the scenario you linked to isn't actually the case in the default setting assumptions of Requiem. It's a pure hypothetical that someone came up with, apparently as a &quot;take that!&quot; to people who think it would be cool to be a vampire. If you want to play a vampire in Chronicles of Darkness but want the character to be the same person as the human who was Embraced, you can just play Requiem. That's how it works already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T23:44:56-08:00","id":1003264,"title":"","content":"Wicked Dead has several non-kindred vampires.<br /> <br /> That said, the scenario linked is a hypothetical and not an actual element of Vampire the Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-15-2016, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T00:30:23-08:00","id":1003271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003166-non-kindred-vampires?p=1003209#post1003209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also how is the Xian different in Korea than the Chinese one I've linked to?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now, please note that what I'm about to write is mostly based on what I've personally come to know and have learned, and other people probably won't agree with me. This is largely because our country's cultural wealth have been decimated by the Occupation by Imperial Japan during the 1930s and WW2. Villages were massacred, relics were stolen, and history books were editted and tampered with so that they support the glory of our Japanese conquerors and prove how we are an inferior race. It's hard to assemble anything that's left. That said...<br /> <br /> The usual word used is Shinseon, spelled with the same Mandarin as Shenxian in the article. Technically, the word refers to a collective of beings - both gods/spirits (Shin/Shen) and immortals/wizards/sages (Seon/Xian), the difference I think was about whether you are immaterial or not, but the Taoism conflate the two concepts anyway.<br /> <br /> Among them we have Shihaeseon, the letters 'shi' meaning 'corpse' and 'hae' meaning 'release'. Basically, remember the Purified from WoD: Immortals? They're almost exactly that. Practitioners of the more mystic and sorcerous side of Taoism that practice something similiar to Hermetic Alchemy to ritually commit suicide and gain immortality. Except 'possessing your corpse' bit. The Shihaeson move their souls to an immortal spirit-body.<br /> <br /> While the Shihaeson are more like powerful sorcerors, the Jiseon start being less mortal and more divine. 'Ji' means 'earth', so Jiseon can be translated as Terrestrial Immortals. They are considered local gods and tutelary deities of the earth, usually of the mountains and lakes and rivers. Sometimes they're seen as government workers of a sort dispatched from the Celestial Bureaucracy. In fact, the whole division between the Terrestrials and the Celestials I'll write now stem from the cultural mix between Korea and China - viewing even gods as part of a vast, centralized government.<br /> <br /> The Cheonseon, 'cheon' meaning 'sky' or 'heaven', are true gods among the immortals. Sometimes said to be even stronger and politically higher-ranked than some actual gods. Thing is, categorizing Shinseon into Terrestrial and Celestial seem to be more of a relatively modern addition (with 'modern' being 'still a few centuries ago')<br /> <br /> Also, one more thing to consider is that in the oldest accounts, (Shin)seon were strictly divine and inhuman in the sense that a human can't become one, period. They were deities who gifted the heroic and the virtuous with immortality. The idea that a mere human could ascend to the heavens through enlightenment is something Taoism imported from Buddhism, and this is probably where people started to differentiate between 'gods' and 'immortals' (though like I said, they were conflated together anyway)<br /> <br /> Hope that helps!<br /> <br /> EDIT: After re-reading the article, I felt the need to point out that the difference lies mostly in the last paragraph I wrote - that Shinseon are traditionally viewed more as gods than ascended humans, but the latter viewpoint isn't necessarily alien to us and have indeed seem to become more popular in current culture and depictions of Shinseon and Taoism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 11-15-2016, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}